---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const UPDATED = '7 November 2026';
const CONTACT = 'support@grosslytics.com';
const h2 = 'mt-12 text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink';
---

<Page title="Terms of service — Grosslytics" description="The terms for using Grosslytics: self-hosting, Hosted Cloud, Lifetime licenses, payments, refunds and responsibilities.">
	<main>
		<article class="prose-g mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-5 pt-14 pb-24 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
			<p class="eyebrow mb-3">Legal</p>
			<h1 class="text-[clamp(34px,5vw,48px)] font-semibold leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Terms of service</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-[15px] text-ink-3">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

			<p class="mt-8">These terms are between you and David Mill, who runs Grosslytics (“we”). By using grosslytics.com, Hosted Cloud, a Lifetime license or the Grosslytics software, you agree to them. Contact: <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>The plans</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
				<li><strong class="text-ink">Self-host:</strong> free and open source under the <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html">AGPL-3.0</a>. You run the software in your own Cloudflare account and are responsible for that account, its costs and its data. The free setup (<code>bun run setup</code>) opens each site’s dashboard only while that site’s home page carries a “Powered by Grosslytics” link to grosslytics.com that search engines may follow; the link is checked daily. Lifetime and Indie Cloud need no link.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-ink">Indie Cloud:</strong> we host it for you, $5.99 a month for up to 100,000 events, after a 14-day trial with no card. When a month’s events reach the limit, or a trial or subscription ends, new events stop being recorded until the next month or until you subscribe. Existing data stays.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-ink">Lifetime:</strong> a one-time payment for a license key and the installer, which sets Grosslytics up in your own Cloudflare account. It includes the updates we publish, priority email support, and a commercial license: you may modify Grosslytics and run it for yourself or your clients without the AGPL’s requirement to publish your changes. It does not include hosting, and the license may not be resold or used to offer Grosslytics as a hosted service to the public.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class={h2}>Payments and refunds</h2>
			<p>Payments are processed by Dodo Payments, which sells as the merchant of record. Indie Cloud renews monthly until you cancel in the billing portal; cancelling stops the next renewal. If something is wrong with a charge, write to us and we will look at it; refunds are made through Dodo Payments to the original payment method.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Your responsibilities</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
				<li>Only add the tracker to sites you control, and tell your visitors about it where the law requires (for example in your own privacy policy).</li>
				<li>Keep your password, API token and webhook secrets private.</li>
				<li>Do not use Grosslytics to break the law, to attack or overload our service, or to track people across sites you do not own.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class={h2}>Your data</h2>
			<p>Data your sites send belongs to you. We process Hosted Cloud data only to provide the service, as described in the <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. If you close your account, write to us and we delete its data within 30 days.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Accuracy</h2>
			<p>Grosslytics reports what it receives. Attribution depends on the visitor ID reaching your payment provider; payment fees are estimates unless the provider reports them; ad blockers, private browsing and bots can make numbers incomplete. Check important figures against your payment provider before acting on them.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Availability and changes</h2>
			<p>We work to keep Hosted Cloud running but do not guarantee uninterrupted service. We may change these terms or the service; we will update the date above, and for paid plans give notice before a change that affects what you pay.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Liability</h2>
			<p>The software and service are provided “as is”. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or lost-profit damages, and our total liability is limited to what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing here limits rights you have by law as a consumer.</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>Ending</h2>
			<p>You can stop using Grosslytics at any time. We may suspend an account that breaks these terms, after telling you why where we can.</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Page>
